  "term": "taijin kyofusho",
  "definition": "Taijin kyofusho is an interpersonal fear centered on offending or upsetting other people. In the supplied source, it is described as a culturally bound syndrome identified in Japan and Korea, though similar cases have also been recognized in other cultures.",
